{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MqWHmjfF4i5csJmAwAutgc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: record-post-close-verification-in-log-d\n3\tdescription: \"A post-close green must be recorded in docs/log.d or docs/iteration only — those paths are excluded from the verdict tree identity, so writing the evidence does not stale the tree the evidence is about\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: d6a44a33-b6fa-4301-8a9d-8a491e68bd04\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\tRecording a verification result is itself a tree change, so on a review-gated\n11\tlane it can invalidate the very reading it records. The escape is that the\n12\tverdict record's tree identity (`kitlib/verdict.py`, WI-579) folds\n13\t`git ls-tree` **excluding** `docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and\n14\t`docs/iteration/`. So write the post-close green into the **log.d fragment\n15\tonly** — never back into the archived spec's `## Deliverable`, which IS in the\n16\tidentity and would move the tree one commit past the figure being claimed.\n17\t\n18\t**Why:** the round-025 finding on WI-579 was exactly this recursion — a full\n19\tsuite driven one commit before the close, then asserted as the closed tree's.\n20\tFixing it by amending the spec would have re-entered the loop; two sessions in a\n21\trow had to re-take the green because the record of the green moved the tree.\n22\t\n23\t**How to apply:** after a close, drive the suite, then append to\n24\t`docs/log.d/<WI>-<slug>.md` and commit with nothing else staged. Verify with\n25\t`verdict.governing_rev(root, \"HEAD\")` — it should still peel back to the close\n26\tcommit, proving the record-only commits did not buy the lane another round.\n27\tCorollary the same asymmetry creates: those paths are excluded from the\n28\tidentity but **not** from the checks, so a green taken before your own log/\n29\ttelemetry commits does not cover them — re-drive at the actual tip.\n30\t\n31\tAlso: the full suite must run on a worktree with `docs/stage` regenerated\n32\t(`derive_stage.py --root .`), since a spine-touching branch moves `drafted` and\n33\ta lane must not commit that trunk-owned generated artifact. Related:\n34\t[[worker-lane-close-ritual-traps]], [[verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers]],\n35\t[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]].\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714c7597-300f-4fed-8cbe-ccdef670ab25","uuid":"d0f23380-ab5a-45e4-956f-0aaa20ff7b2f","timestamp":"2026-09-03T11:33:22.388Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/record-post-close-verification-in-log-d.md","content":"---\nname: record-post-close-verification-in-log-d\ndescription: \"A post-close green must be recorded in docs/log.d or docs/iteration only — those paths are excluded from the verdict tree identity, so writing the evidence does not stale the tree the evidence is about\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: d6a44a33-b6fa-4301-8a9d-8a491e68bd04\n---\n\nRecording a verification result is itself a tree change, so on a review-gated\nlane it can invalidate the very reading it records. The escape is that the\nverdict record's tree identity (`kitlib/verdict.py`, WI-579) folds\n`git ls-tree` **excluding** `docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and\n`docs/iteration/`. So write the post-close green into the **log.d fragment\nonly** — never back into the archived spec's `## Deliverable`, which IS in the\nidentity and would move the tree one commit past the figure being claimed.\n\n**Why:** the round-025 finding on WI-579 was exactly this recursion — a full\nsuite driven one commit before the close, then asserted as the closed tree's.\nFixing it by amending the spec would have re-entered the loop; two sessions in a\nrow had to re-take the green because the record of the green moved the tree.\n\n**How to apply:** after a close, drive the suite, then append to\n`docs/log.d/<WI>-<slug>.md` and commit with nothing else staged. Verify with\n`verdict.governing_rev(root, \"HEAD\")` — it should still peel back to the close\ncommit, proving the record-only commits did not buy the lane another round.\nCorollary the same asymmetry creates: those paths are excluded from the\nidentity but **not** from the checks, so a green taken before your own log/\ntelemetry commits does not cover them — re-drive at the actual tip.\n\nAlso: the full suite must run on a worktree with `docs/stage` regenerated\n(`derive_stage.py --root .`), since a spine-touching branch moves `drafted` and\na lane must not commit that trunk-owned generated artifact. Related:\n[[worker-lane-close-ritual-traps]], [[verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers]],\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]].\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
