{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegS7DUDxuyko2E4cDeQX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1441,"cache_read_input_tokens":183025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1441},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714c7597-300f-4fed-8cbe-ccdef670ab25","uuid":"5c3c8f02-3bbe-4005-9ea0-65220e3a4237","request_id":"req_011CegS7CDKENVPKCjFFAB8A"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegS7DUDxuyko2E4cDeQX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013vtr6u8pXbeRakGt6WHWDT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan.md","content":"---\nname: tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan\ndescription: \"A regression asserting `derivation(...) == []` can be reading silence, not agreement — check the fixture actually produces the evidence the derivation scans before trusting the assertion\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nA derivation that returns a falsey value both when it READ the evidence and\nfound nothing, and when it could not read the evidence at all, makes every\n`assert f(...) == []` ambiguous — including the regression written to prove the\nbug closed. Confirm the fixture really produces what the scan looks for, and\nprefer a derivation with three answers (`None` = cannot say, `[]` = read it,\nnothing found, a list = these) over two.\n\n**Why:** WI-579 round 034. `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` scans\n`base..HEAD` for the assigned WIs' `WI:` trailers first. The round-033\nregression `test_a_stale_owed_marker_over_served_evidence_redraws_nothing` used\na fixture (`rounds_repo`) that commits no `WI:` trailer at all, so its premise\nline — `== []`, commented \"both declared phases were served\" — was asserting\nsilence. That hollow premise is why the same round's fix could invert the C2\nresume contract (a parked review round dropped, another BUILD run) with the\ntest still green, red for five commits.\n\n**How to apply:** when a test asserts an empty/falsey result from an evidence\nscan, first assert the NON-empty case on the same fixture, or drive the fixture\nto prove the scan has input. When splitting a conflated falsey value, expect the\nold regressions to break on their premises — that is the bug surfacing, so fix\nthe fixture, never the assertion. Related: the paired lesson that a smoke-tier\ngap hides this: the end-to-end test that caught it was in\n`tests/conftest.py` `SLOW_MODULES`, so put the new guard in an in-process\nmodule that the commit bar actually runs.\n\nRelated: [[record-post-close-verification-in-log-d]] (its corollary bit here\ntoo — the round-033 close scheduled its unfiltered green for \"the follow-up\ncommit\", and every follow-up that could carry it also invalidated it; drive at\nthe tip AFTER the last tree-changing commit),\n[[verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1441,"cache_read_input_tokens":183025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1441},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714c7597-300f-4fed-8cbe-ccdef670ab25","uuid":"005647ab-4e8f-4004-931e-03e021bc8dc3","request_id":"req_011CegS7CDKENVPKCjFFAB8A"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013vtr6u8pXbeRakGt6WHWDT","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714c7597-300f-4fed-8cbe-ccdef670ab25","uuid":"775e39d3-36ac-4d90-8e38-380345ea7611","timestamp":"2026-09-03T11:33:40.265Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan.md","content":"---\nname: tests-that-pass-on-an-empty-scan\ndescription: \"A regression asserting `derivation(...) == []` can be reading silence, not agreement — check the fixture actually produces the evidence the derivation scans before trusting the assertion\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 714c7597-300f-4fed-8cbe-ccdef670ab25\n---\n\nA derivation that returns a falsey value both when it READ the evidence and\nfound nothing, and when it could not read the evidence at all, makes every\n`assert f(...) == []` ambiguous — including the regression written to prove the\nbug closed. Confirm the fixture really produces what the scan looks for, and\nprefer a derivation with three answers (`None` = cannot say, `[]` = read it,\nnothing found, a list = these) over two.\n\n**Why:** WI-579 round 034. `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` scans\n`base..HEAD` for the assigned WIs' `WI:` trailers first. The round-033\nregression `test_a_stale_owed_marker_over_served_evidence_redraws_nothing` used\na fixture (`rounds_repo`) that commits no `WI:` trailer at all, so its premise\nline — `== []`, commented \"both declared phases were served\" — was asserting\nsilence. That hollow premise is why the same round's fix could invert the C2\nresume contract (a parked review round dropped, another BUILD run) with the\ntest still green, red for five commits.\n\n**How to apply:** when a test asserts an empty/falsey result from an evidence\nscan, first assert the NON-empty case on the same fixture, or drive the fixture\nto prove the scan has input. When splitting a conflated falsey value, expect the\nold regressions to break on their premises — that is the bug surfacing, so fix\nthe fixture, never the assertion. Related: the paired lesson that a smoke-tier\ngap hides this: the end-to-end test that caught it was in\n`tests/conftest.py` `SLOW_MODULES`, so put the new guard in an in-process\nmodule that the commit bar actually runs.\n\nRelated: [[record-post-close-verification-in-log-d]] (its corollary bit here\ntoo — the round-033 close scheduled its unfiltered green for \"the follow-up\ncommit\", and every follow-up that could carry it also invalidated it; drive at\nthe tip AFTER the last tree-changing commit),\n[[verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
