{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegS8kFRCDj2PsDFpsKpf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-579 is closed on a green I produced. The round-033 rework was already addressed — but it had closed on a claim, not a measurement.\n\n## What I found\n\nThe round-033 close scheduled Done-when 5's unfiltered green for \"the follow-up commit.\" Two follow-ups landed, both recording only the smoke bar. So the newest driven full-suite reading was `ddd08d67`, three tree-changing commits behind a spec sitting in `archive/work/complete/` asserting that criterion.\n\nDriven at the tip, it was **red**: `test_reviewer_outage_parks_review_owed_then_resume_draws_the_round`. A per-commit bisect put it on `7ed5a136` — the round-033 finding-2 fix itself — red for five commits.\n\n**The defect.** `review_owed_by_evidence` answered `[]` both for *read the evidence, nothing owed* and for *could not read it*. The second is reachable on the shipped path: `default_base` merge-bases to HEAD when the primary checkout is the lane branch, so a resumed run scans an empty range and reads every assigned WI as unbuilt. Round 033 correctly deleted the marker OR-arm that had been papering over it, and the conflation underneath became load-bearing — a parked review round dropped, another BUILD run. The C2 contract inverted.\n\n**Fixed** by finishing round 033's own antidote one level down: three answers instead of two (`None` = cannot say), and the resume re-*asks* the derivation at the base the owed-marker carries rather than answering for it. The marker still decides nothing; the stale-marker redraw stays closed.\n\n**The regression written to close finding 2 was passing on an empty scan.** `rounds_repo` commits no `WI:` trailer, so its \"both phases served\" premise asserted silence. I fixed the fixture, not the assertion. The new guard went into a smoke-tier module — the end-to-end test that caught this is one `SLOW_MODULES` drops, which is how five commits landed red under a green commit bar.\n\n## Also corrected\n\n- The fragment's top-matter `Deferred open items: none` had been false since round 033, whose own section hands the owner a finding. **OI-83** (coordinator runs modules imported at launch) and **OI-84** (the resumed-run base; three other blind readers this fix leaves standing) now carry it. `gen_open_items` ARM 4 structurally cannot reach that case — its declared weakness, met in the wild.\n- The Deliverable's `\"at the closing tip\"` bar figure now names its rev. A claim pinned to a moving referent is false the moment the referent moves.\n\n## Verification\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Full unfiltered @ `566b40e6` | **3359 passed, 25 skipped, 0 failed in 608.65 s** |\n| Commit bar | 1520 passed, 8 skipped in 36.57 s; enforcer 50.8 s / 60 s |\n| Tree identity | `ca1b3004…` byte-identical at close and record commit |\n\nThat last row is the point: the green was recorded in `docs/log.d/` (outside the identity fold), verified with this WI's own mechanism, so the record does not stale the reading — the durable form of what round 033 tried to do with \"recorded in the follow-up commit.\"\n\nBoth new tests were driven against the pre-fix module; both bite, the behaviour arm independently of the shape arm. Tree clean, no root coordination truth touched, no approval act in the delta. **The lane is closed and owes a fresh REVIEW-A round** — the tree moved past round 033's reviewed tree, so its verdict no longer governs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":185679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714c7597-300f-4fed-8cbe-ccdef670ab25","uuid":"aa181a6f-3d80-4c44-a72b-a69e4ab8e860","request_id":"req_011CegS8jDuHpqLpJmk7Fm3u"}
